  "limitations": [
    "Annotations were produced by Codex and have not been reviewed by the user or a human annotator. They are not a human gold dataset.",
    "The small purposive sample is dominated by point-to-point chat and discussions that should be ignored. No may_reply or should_wait positive coverage was established.",
    "All must_reply cases used the explicit-invitation hard gate. Provider judgments in this run covered only should_ignore cases, so the reported recall does not measure positive judge semantics.",
    "Eligibility standardized cooldown, budget and recent-activity gates. These results do not reconstruct live dynamic sending decisions or authorize production activation.",
    "Capture-time persona, permissions and policies were applied to historical message order. Earlier policy and authorization changes were not reconstructed.",
    "Overlapping context windows are correlated. Wilson intervals and p95 are descriptive for this small sample, without population-level accuracy or latency claims.",
    "Known-bot exclusion followed stored event flags. Automated-account utterances may remain among the recorded participants.",
    "Images and other media were represented by type markers, and deidentification may remove some contextual detail.",
    "The production database and configuration were read-only inputs. The replay and all raw evidence were isolated in a root-restricted temporary directory."
  ]
